{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-53b4d968-b76c-43e9-8ddc-b0d022e92031","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f58742a71559060","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-eskf3xkk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nConvert all reconciliation error log calls in the rhods-operator manager binary that embed resource name or namespace in unstructured message strings into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), add `resourceKind` as a structured field across all controller tiers and action files, and migrate the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from its non-standard field names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the standard camelCase convention. This makes reconciliation error logs queryable by resource name, namespace, and kind across all controllers in the manager binary, and adds a CI guard so the convention holds for future code.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's five controller tiers: the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, and the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup). Track audit coverage in a checklist; confirm the actual share of calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate: 75%).\n- Convert every audited call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs using the fields `name` and `namespace`, removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n- Migrate DSCI controller structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`; no references to the old field names may remain.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in: service controllers, the module controller and its module handlers, all action files, and the DSC and 8 component controllers (for the latter, kind is implied by the controller name — this is a queryability enhancement).\n- Cover all 15 action files across 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) correctly: emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious namespace value.\n- Add a repo-wide CI lint rule or static analysis check that flags any `log.Error` call embedding name/namespace in the message text or missing the required structured fields.\n- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via a test logger for the converted call sites.\n- Backwards-compatibility verification per the strategy NFR: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and that existing log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update text-based alert rules that rely on current message-string patterns.\n- Rollback/release-notes handling for the DSCI field-name migration: document the change with before/after query examples so operators using the old field names can update saved queries (full migration guide authoring belongs to the convention documentation effort; this epic supplies the release-notes entry).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given any manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, the updated call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis passing with zero flagged `log.Error` calls across the manager binary.\n- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) — measured by unit tests asserting the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` remain.\n- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error, the log entry includes `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value for each of the 5 service controllers.\n- Given an action file error log in any of the 4 tiers, the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n- Given a module controller error log for any of the 8 module handlers, the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests over test logger output.\n- Given a DSC or component controller reconciliation error, the entry includes `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests across the DSC controller and all 8 component controllers.\n- Given a cluster-scoped resource (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) reconciliation error, the entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty — measured by unit tests confirming no spurious namespace value.\n- Given a sample reconciliation error before and after the change, the before/after log output comparison shows the structured fields present, and the production log consumer stack ingests both formats without configuration changes — measured by a dev-cluster test-build verification with the consumer stack configured and existing alert queries confirmed to still match (after SRE/Support-coordinated updates where needed).\n- Given the DSCI field-name migration, a rollback path exists (revert of the migration commit) and the release-notes entry with before/after query examples is drafted — measured by review of the release-notes draft alongside the merge.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — manager binary portion\n- [P0] DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`)\n- [P0] All service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` as a structured field\n- [P0] All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module action files)\n- [P0] Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields (8 module handlers)\n- [P1] DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35147,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-baa925d7539d371f","agent_id":"a4fab90d3e09492e9","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"bbd70427-2d8e-4463-9190-ba7ea0120a84","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:10:50.842Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
