{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3439513e-20dc-481a-b4e3-d2689b6e0bc5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80a8df2768dd68f0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-eskf3xkk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Standardize cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nApply the same reconciliation error log standardization to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary: convert message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and add `resourceKind` to the error logs of the three multi-cloud infrastructure controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine). These controllers already receive `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger via the shared reconciler pattern, so the remaining work is converting any message-embedded identity and adding the kind field. This epic is scoped to the cloudmanager binary only and can be scheduled independently of the manager-binary work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths of the cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine), which are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern.\n- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs.\n- Add unit tests asserting `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` presence and correctness via a test logger for the cloudmanager controllers.\n- Comply with the repo-wide CI lint rule that flags `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n- Apply the same backwards-compatibility verification approach as the manager binary where feasible: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming log consumers ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error, the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output for each of the three controllers.\n- Given a cloudmanager reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, the updated call uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the repo CI lint rule / static analysis passing with zero flagged `log.Error` calls in the cloudmanager binary.\n- Given a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error before and after the change, the before/after log output comparison shows the structured fields present and the log consumer ingesting both formats without configuration changes — measured by inspection of captured test-build log output.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields\n- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — cloudmanager binary portion\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36833,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-baa925d7539d371f","agent_id":"a4fab90d3e09492e9","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"902906ef-27a0-4b7