nd is not penalized. Three minor issues\n38\tfound; no critical or major issues.\n39\t\n40\t## Criterion Details\n41\t\n42\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n43\tAll 8 HLRs (6 P0, 2 P1) map to at least one epic; the traceability matrix in the summary matches each\n44\tepic's HLR Traceability section exactly (the split HLR-1 conversion is correctly divided into manager\n45\t(E001) and cloudmanager (E002) portions, and both portions appear in the respective epics). Priority\n46\tinheritance: E001 and E002 are P0 and block no P0 work other than the P1 docs-authoring epic (exempt);\n47\tE003's P1 derives correctly from the strategy's Major Jira priority. Priority collapse check: the P1\n48\t\"DSC/component controller resourceKind\" HLR is bundled into E001, but this is the same one-line change\n49\tat the same log call sites and test surfaces as the P0 conversion — incidental polish, not a deferrable\n50\tfeature on a separate surface — and the summary explicitly justifies the bundling. Correctly handled.\n51\t\n52\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n53\tNo circular dependencies; both edges (E001 → E003, E002 → E003) are Rule 11 docs-authoring edges and are\n54\tpresent in both the mermaid diagram (correct dependency → dependent arrow direction) and E003's\n55\tfrontmatter `dependencies`; E001/E002 frontmatter dependencies are empty, matching the edge-free\n56\tparallel design. E001 ∥ E002 is justified under rule 15 (same repo but architecturally distinct binaries\n57\twith disjoint controller sets; the strategy's open cloudmanager release-phasing question makes\n58\tindependent schedulability valuable). Critical path length 2 fits the S-strategy heuristic (1-2). No\n59\tkonflux/license-validation epics exist, so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are vacuous. No\n60\tconditional branch files. Scanned epic content for uncaptured data/artifact dependencies: the only\n61\tcross-epic reference is E002's lint-rule AC (see minor issue below) — it is a verification-tooling\n62\treference