checked\n87\tvalues against strategy content: E001 `change_specificity: 1` (exact field names, file inventory,\n88\tpaths), `pattern_precedent: 1` (in-repo structured-logging precedent confirmed by SME input),\n89\t`human_process_gates: -1` (the NFR's dev-cluster verification with production log consumer stack and\n90\tSRE/Support coordination is a genuine human gate), `open_questions: 0` (remaining questions affect\n91\taudit effort and rollout verification, not the implementation approach) — all justified. E003's\n92\t`open_questions: -1` and `human_process_gates: -1` are correct (the PM/Observability additional-fields\n93\tdecision directly changes the doc's content; technical review is mandated). E002's\n94\t`human_process_gates: 0` is borderline (see minor issue below) but defensibly rationale'd. Arithmetic\n95\tand thresholds not checked per instructions (computed by pipeline).\n96\t\n97\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n98\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy's proposed ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are present:\n99\tthe DSCI field-name migration (a replacement) has a rollback AC (revert of the migration commit) plus a\n100\trelease-notes entry with before/after query examples in E001; the docs-authoring epic E003 has the\n101\ttechnical-review-against-implementation AC; no konflux chain exists, so no build-pipeline AC applies.\n102\tNo non-testable schedule-constraint ACs were found (the SRE-coordination items are verification\n103\tactivities with measurable outcomes, not timing constraints misfiled as ACs). No epic body references\n104\tsibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references use descriptive phrases (\"the manager binary\", \"the\n105\tconvention documentation effort\"), which is correct for Jira-bound artifacts.\n106\t\n107\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n108\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: every strategy acceptance criterion maps to an epic AC (embedded-\n109\tidentity conversion, DSCI migration, service-controller resourceKind, all 15 action files across 4\n110\ttiers, cloudmanager controllers, cluster-scoped resources, the documented convention); all four\n111\tstrategy risks are carried forward (audit checklist + CI lint in E001, log-consumer regression\n112\tverification as an E001 AC, COO publication + tracking issues in E003, single-release DSCI migration in\n113\tE001's AC and the summary's Health Warnings); all four open questions are explicitly dispositioned in\n114\tthe summary's Investigation Assessment and carried into epic scope/ACs where relevant. The NFRs are\n115\taddressed (backwards-compatibility verification in E001/E002; performance requires no verification per\n116\tthe strategy). The strategy's \"Design doc: to be created\" item (three-problem diagnosis, before/after\n117\texamples, DSCI migration guide) is subsumed by E003's guideline outline. External-operator scope is\n118\tcorrectly excluded from implementation epics per platform policy overlay 0008, with the controllable\n119\tdeliverable (publication + tracking issues) in E003. Out-of-scope items are respected. No\n120\tdocs-authoring gap: the strategy's HLR P1 explicitly requires the guideline and E003 delivers it.\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f855ef2a480931a","agent_id":"a96558e77e1b7cd9e","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"187b0fa1-ee6f-4a41-896a-26d0c3790507","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:17:29.514Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0b8fae5127935d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
