{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b47393dbf09c6bc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8010\n11\t\n12\tOperator reconciliation log standardization with structured resource context.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: although the strategy is S-sized, single-component (rhods-operator) and single-team for\n17\tcode changes, the scope spans two distinct work-product streams — mechanical code conversion across the\n18\tmanager and cloudmanager binaries, and substantive content authoring (a new contribution guideline that\n19\tdocuments the convention, includes before/after code examples and a DSCI key-migration guide, and is\n20\tpublished for external operator adoption). Per Step 0's multiple-work-streams escape condition, the strategy\n21\tproceeds to full decomposition. Not documentation-only: rhods-operator requires code changes.\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n26\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 | Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context | Implementation | ODH Operator team | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8010-E002 | Standardize cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs to structured resource context | Implementation | ODH Operator team | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8010-E003 | Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention | Implementation (docs-authoring) | ODH Operator team | P1 |\n30\t\n31\t## Dependency DAG\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t    RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n36\t    RHAISTRAT-8010-E002 --> RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t## DAG Justification\n40\t\n41\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n42\t|------|------|-----------|\n43\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | 15 | Same repo, architecturally distinct binaries with separate controller sets (manager vs. cloudmanager); no shared artifacts being built. Merge proximity is a coordination risk, not a dependency. Keeping them separate also honors the open release-phasing question for cloudmanager — either epic can be scheduled independently. E002's conversion AC is measured by its own static-analysis scan of the cloudmanager sources rather than by the repo-wide CI lint rule authored in the manager-binary work, so neither epic's verification depends on the other landing first. |\n44\t| E001 → E003 | 11 | `docs-authoring` epic is blocked by all Implementation epics; the guideline documents the convention as implemented, including before/after examples drawn from the converted code. |\n45\t| E002 → E003 | 11 | Same rule — the guideline covers the convention across both binaries. |\n46\t\n47\t## Component Mapping\n48\t\n49\tThe strategy names a single affected component, **rhods-operator**. That name does not appear verbatim in\n50\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`; the closest canonical Jira component is **OpenShift AI Productization**, which\n51\tcovers the rhods-operator (red-hat-data-services/rhods-operator, midstream opendatahub-operator) work owned by\n52\tthe ODH Operator team. All three epics use `OpenShift AI Productization`; submit.py would silently strip a\n53\tnon-canonical value such as \"rhods-operator\".\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n56\t\n57\t| HLR | Priority | Epic |\n58\t|-----|----------|------|\n59\t| Convert message-embedded resource identity in reconciliation error logs to structured `name`/`namespace` KV pairs | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001, RHAISTRAT-8010-E002 |\n60\t| Migrate DSCI controller from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase convention | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 |\n61\t| Service controller error logs include `resourceKind` | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 |\n62\t| All 15 action-file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across 4 tiers | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 |\n63\t| Cloudmanager controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E002 |\n64\t| Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 |\n65\t| DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` | P1 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E001 |\n66\t| Document the convention as a contribution guideline and publish for external adoption | P1 | RHAISTRAT-8010-E003 |\n67\t\n68\tFull coverage: all 8 HLRs map to at least one epic. The P1 HLR (DSC/component controller `resourceKind`) is\n69\tbundled into E001 rather than split: it touches the same log call sites, files, and test surfaces as the P0\n70\tconversion work — it is a queryability enhancement incidental to the same implementation, not a deferrable\n71\tfeature on a separate surface.\n72\t\n73\t## Epic Boundary Rationale\n74\t\n75\t- **E001 vs. E002**: same component and team, but manager and cloudmanager are architecturally distinct\n76\t  sub-systems (two binaries, disjoint controller sets, different deployment targets — OpenShift vs. EKS/AKS/\n77\t  CoreWeave). Split along the sub-system boundary per Rule 2; the strategy's open question on cloudmanager\n78\t  release phasing makes independent planning valuable.\n79\t- **E001 vs. E003 / E002 vs. E003**: code implementation vs. substantive content authoring are different\n80\t  work-product types with different review criteria (Rule 2). The guideline is a new doc topic with authored\n81\t  content (convention spec, rationale, before/after examples, migration guide), not an incidental touch-up.\n82\t- **CI lint rule** (flagging `log.Error` calls with embedded identity or missing required fields) is folded\n83\t  into E001's scope: it is repo-wide CI configuration that enforces the conversion E001 performs — same\n84\t  change, same review cycle, no independent user value.\n85\t- **COO (Loki/Tempo Operator) adoption**: no epic. Per platform policy overlay 0008, RHOAI does not install,\n86\t  manage, or control external operators; adoption is voluntary and at the COO team's discretion. The\n87\t  deliverable RHOAI controls is publishing the convention and filing tracking issues, which is E003 scope.\n88\t\n89\t## Investigation Assessment\n90\t\n91\tNo Investigation epics. Each open question was evaluated against \"does the answer change which downstream\n92\tepics exist or what they do?\":\n93\t\n94\t- *Additional fields beyond name/namespace/kind* (PM/Observability): changes the convention doc's content at\n95\t  most; the required field set for the code work is fixed by the HLRs and Staff Engineer input. Captured as an\n96\t  open question on E003.\n97\t- *Which alerts rely on message-string patterns* (SRE/Support): resolved during the regression-verification\n98\t  step the strategy already prescribes; captured as an acceptance criterion on E001/E002, not an epic.\n99\t- *Cloudmanager release phasing* (PM): a scheduling decision — the work exists either way. Handled by keeping\n100\t  E002 edge-free (independently schedulable); noted in Health Warnings.\n101\t- *Actual percentage of embedded-identity log calls*: the audit is the first implementation step of E001; the\n102\t  conversion scope (\"all reconciliation error log call sites\") is unchanged by the number.\n103\t\n104\t## Health Warnings\n105\t\n106\t- **Release phasing (non-blocking)**: cloudmanager (E002) may follow in a subsequent release per the open\n107\t  question owned by PM/ODH Operator team. The DAG intentionally leaves E002 parallel so either answer is\n108\t  supported; if deferred, E003's blocker set still includes it.\n109\t- **Log consumer regression risk**: text-based alert rules that match current message strings may break.\n110\t  Mitigation (dev-cluster verification with production log consumer stack, SRE/Support coordination) is an\n111\t  acceptance criterion on E001; the DSCI field-name migration should land in a single release to avoid\n112\t  long-term query inconsistency.\n113\t- **Process gates pending**: Architecture Review and other prerequisites are marked \"Pending human review\" in\n114\t  the strategy — standard sign-off, not structural unknowns.\n115\t- **Priority note**: the strategy's proposed acceptance criteria state they \"require PM/Engineering\n116\t  validation\"; ACs below are derived from the strategy as written.\n117\t\n118\t## Tiered Delivery\n119\t\n120\tNot applicable. The only external dependency (COO team adoption) is voluntary and outside RHOAI control by\n121\tpolicy; no RHOAI work is gated on it. All implementation work is independent of external timing.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a47cdf0ccbc52b","agent_id":"af2122881aee379b0","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"ca97ac33-e76e-426b-9190-61e50a4ba9f0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:19:45.603Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b47393dbf09c6bc6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
