{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-919ba36304607080","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs to structured\n4\t  resource context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tApply the same reconciliation error log standardization to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary: convert message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and add `resourceKind` to the error logs of the three multi-cloud infrastructure controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine). These controllers already receive `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger via the shared reconciler pattern, so the remaining work is converting any message-embedded identity and adding the kind field. This epic is scoped to the cloudmanager binary only and can be scheduled independently of the manager-binary work.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths of the cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine), which are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern.\n39\t- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs.\n41\t- Add unit tests asserting `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` presence and correctness via a test logger for the cloudmanager controllers.\n42\t- Comply with the repo-wide CI lint rule (authored alongside the manager-binary conversion) that flags `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields; if this epic lands before that rule exists, demonstrate compliance with an equivalent static-analysis scan of the cloudmanager sources.\n43\t- Apply the same backwards-compatibility verification approach as the manager binary where feasible: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming log consumers ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error, the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output for each of the three controllers.\n48\t- Given a cloudmanager reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, the updated call uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by a static-analysis scan of the cloudmanager controller sources (e.g., grep over `log.Error` call sites) reporting zero calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields; this check is runnable independently of the repo-wide CI lint rule authored in the manager-binary conversion, and once that rule is in place, CI passes with zero flagged `log.Error` calls in the cloudmanager binary.\n49\t- Given a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error before and after the change, the before/after log output comparison shows the structured fields present and the log consumer ingesting both formats without configuration changes — measured by inspection of captured test-build log output.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- [P0] All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields\n54\t- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — cloudmanager binary portion\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a47cdf0ccbc52b","agent_id":"af2122881aee379b0","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"bd53f888-f51c-4e62-a5ac-6b74af67ef2a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:19:49.697Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-919ba36304607080","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
