{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b560d7d1e6f2d947","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAuthor the structured reconciliation log field convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development in the rhods-operator, and publish it for voluntary adoption by external operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per platform policy overlay 0008. The guideline specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale aligned with controller-runtime conventions, the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`), before/after code examples drawn from the completed conversion, and a DSCI key-migration guide with before/after query examples.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\tContent outline for the guideline:\n40\t\n41\t- Required structured fields for reconciliation error logs: `name`, `namespace` (with the cluster-scoped-resource rule: `namespace` omitted or empty, never spurious), and `resourceKind`.\n42\t- camelCase field-naming rationale and alignment with controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions.\n43\t- The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, DSCI non-standard key names, and missing `resourceKind`.\n44\t- Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs, taken from the converted controller and action-file code.\n45\t- DSCI key-migration guide: before/after Loki/CloudWatch query examples for operators with saved queries filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`.\n46\t- Guidance for new controller development, including how the CI lint rule enforces the convention.\n47\t- Open question to be settled during authoring (owner: PM / Observability team): whether the convention should recommend fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category), weighing added utility against log volume. The required field set is fixed; any additional fields are recommendations only.\n48\t- Publication for external adoption: publish the convention where external operator teams can consume it and file tracking issues in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects. Adoption remains at the COO team's discretion per platform policy — no RHOAI-side enforcement or dependency.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis — measured by review of the published document against this outline.\n53\t- The guideline includes before/after code examples for the conversion and a DSCI key-migration section with before/after query examples — measured by review of the document content.\n54\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented conversion (field names, examples, and cluster-scoped behavior match the shipped code) — measured by a documented review by an engineer familiar with the implementation.\n55\t- The convention is published for external consumption and tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects — measured by links to the published convention and the filed issues.\n56\t- A decision on recommended-but-optional fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` is recorded in the guideline (either included as recommendations or explicitly excluded with rationale) — measured by the decision appearing in the reviewed document.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- [P1] Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a47cdf0ccbc52b","agent_id":"af2122881aee379b0","session_id":"b85c52ef-139b-4b48-a119-7718fd584270","uuid":"16acfb1b-e77a-4b01-823e-52af7db50209","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:19:50.379Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b560d7d1e6f2d947","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
